      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Additional idea to account for updating avatars uploaded in this manner:\nAvatars that are pending can be downloaded and tested via the existing build and test function utilized by the VRCSDK.  The avatar can then be denied if needed, or approved as either an update or a completely new avatar.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-11-09T18:08:54.394Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This will be useful for commissioned avatars.\nCurrently, the only way for an artist or avatar maker to upload an avatar to a customer is to either give them the full unity project, or ask for their VRChat credentials.  The latter is obviously risky and advised against by the VRChat team.\nAn \"upload to other User\" option would solve this nicely.  The creator would set the option, type in the username of the recipient, and it would then go into pending for said user.  The user can then either approve or deny the upload.\nFor security, this system would be set to auto-deny by default, and require turning on from the VRChat website.",
